WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:16.807
Unit seven: Listening: Conversations. Today you will follow campus conversations and understand tone and intention.

4
00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:19.632
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.660
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:25.692
Conversation.

7
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:29.275
Conversation means a talk between two people.

8
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:31.523
Listen to the conversation.

9
00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:35.152
Your turn. Say: Conversation.

10
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.198
Conversation.

11
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:40.905
Advisor.

12
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:44.891
Advisor means a person who gives academic help.

13
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.065
She meets her advisor.

14
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.268
Your turn. Say: Advisor.

15
00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.169
Advisor.

16
00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:56.104
Registration.

17
00:00:57.117 --> 00:00:59.755
Registration means signing up for classes.

18
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.373
Registration closes today.

19
00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:05.705
Your turn. Say: Registration.

20
00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.719
Registration.

21
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:11.426
Concern.

22
00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:13.929
Concern means a worry.

23
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.389
He has a concern about the fee.

24
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:19.752
Your turn. Say: Concern.

25
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.601
Concern.

26
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.177
Reason.

27
00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:28.345
Reason means why something happens.

28
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.334
Listen for the reason.

29
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.068
Your turn. Say: Reason.

30
00:01:35.933 --> 00:01:36.865
Reason.

31
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:38.641
Attitude.

32
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.451
Attitude means how someone feels about something.

33
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.411
Notice her attitude.

34
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:47.855
Your turn. Say: Attitude.

35
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.585
Attitude.

36
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.502
Solution.

37
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:56.841
Solution means a way to solve a problem.

38
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.055
They agree on a solution.

39
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.616
Your turn. Say: Solution.

40
00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.584
Solution.

41
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.293
Replay.

42
00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:11.562
Replay means to hear a short part again.

43
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.138
You may hear a replay of one line.

44
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.170
Your turn. Say: Replay.

45
00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:20.918
Replay.

46
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:25.164
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:29.061
Visal, what happens in a conversation task?

48
00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:43.031
You hear a short talk between two people, often a student and a staff member. Questions ask about the problem, the reason, the speaker's feeling and what happens next.

49
00:02:44.117 --> 00:02:45.663
How do I follow the story?

50
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:56.264
Listen for the problem first, then the suggestions, then the final decision. Notes of three or four words help you remember each step.

51
00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.955
How do I understand tone?

52
00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:11.944
Listen to the voice, not only the words. A rising or falling voice can show surprise, worry or relief, and a replayed line usually has a question about its meaning.

53
00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.972
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.817 --> 00:03:19.848
Grammar focus: Strategy: problem, solution, decision.

55
00:03:20.148 --> 00:03:21.451
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.334
The student is worried about missing the registration deadline.

57
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.376
The advisor suggests that she fill in an online form.

58
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:36.538
Follow the problem, the solution and the decision in order. Notice the tone of voice, and answer from what you heard.

59
00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:40.563
Be careful! Don't say: I write every word I hear.

60
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.674
Say: I write short notes only.

61
00:03:44.974 --> 00:03:45.998
Short notes.

62
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.301
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.833
At the Advisor's Office.

64
00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.734
A student visits her advisor before registration closes.

65
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:59.395
She is worried because one course is already full.

66
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.468
The advisor suggests joining the waiting list online.

67
00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.733
The student feels relieved and thanks her.

68
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:10.325
She promises to fill in the form that afternoon.

69
00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:15.191
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.885
In a conversation, listen first for the blank.

71
00:04:19.185 --> 00:04:22.572
A, title. B, problem. C, date.

72
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.982
The answer is B: problem.

73
00:04:29.117 --> 00:04:31.012
The student is worried about blank.

74
00:04:31.312 --> 00:04:35.476
A, a lost bag. B, her hair. C, a full course.

75
00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:41.056
The answer is C: a full course.

76
00:04:42.217 --> 00:04:44.216
The advisor suggests blank.

77
00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:49.203
A, joining a waiting list. B, leaving the university. C, paying more.

78
00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.765
The answer is A: joining a waiting list.

79
00:04:56.917 --> 00:04:58.974
How does the student feel at the end?

80
00:04:59.274 --> 00:05:02.951
A, bored. B, relieved. C, angry.

81
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.372
The answer is B: relieved.

82
00:05:09.517 --> 00:05:11.052
Notes should be blank.

83
00:05:11.352 --> 00:05:16.085
A, full sentences. B, in another language only. C, short.

84
00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:21.389
The answer is C: short.

85
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.728
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:26.583 --> 00:05:28.966
How do you follow a campus conversation?

87
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.157
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:39.457 --> 00:05:52.933
I listen first for the problem, then for the solutions the speakers suggest. I write short notes, and I pay attention to the tone of voice to understand feelings. At the end I think about what will happen next.

89
00:05:53.233 --> 00:05:55.174
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:56.083 --> 00:06:01.290
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: problem, solution, decision.

91
00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.355
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:06:06.655 --> 00:06:09.087
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

93
00:06:09.387 --> 00:06:11.749
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

